# Line endings. Text files are stored with LF in the repository and checked
# out with LF on every platform, whatever core.autocrlf says. Windows scripts
# are the exception: they are still stored with LF, but checked out with CRLF,
# because cmd.exe can misparse labels and `goto` in LF-only batch files.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary files: never touch their bytes.
*.icns binary
*.ico binary
*.jar binary
*.otf binary
*.png binary
*.ttf binary
*.webp binary
